{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p paper\ncat > paper/OUTLINE.md <<'EOF'\n# Paper outline and evidence map\n\n1. Abstract: finite, context-dependent arithmetic editing; 6.73% vs 4.05% protected change; 60.78% breadth transfer; no universal conclusion.\n2. Introduction: define preservation scope; motivate computed facts; introduce controlled design figure; preview main results; three contributions and roadmap.\n3. Related work: locality/propagation (Cohen, Qin, Zhang, Gupta); restricted FT and routing (Gangadhar); arithmetic mechanisms (Nikankin, Kantamneni); operational belief depth (Wang, Slocum). Use archived metadata and supplied review, without priority claims.\n4. Methodology: literal vs semantic protection sets; recursive oracle; fixed model/interface; loss and optimizer; datasets/baselines; strict metrics and conditional clustered uncertainty.\n5. Results: primary table from REPORT.md/summary.csv and cluster_intervals.json; paired contrasts; strata and sham; context table; robustness edits and distributional drift; separate API control.\n6. Discussion: interpretation, finite scope, weak capability baselines, small seeds, replay and token confounds, post-hoc analyses, broader implications.\n7. Conclusion: exact efficacy is attainable, isolation absent in tested weight edits, context dependence limits belief claims; targeted follow-up.\n8. Appendix: baseline counts, complete secondary results, seed variation, language drift, compute/reproduction/provenance, additional diagnostic plots.\n\nVisuals: original vector scope/design diagram; primary result table; strata table; context table; secondary and drift tables; original experiment operand map and development trajectories.\nReview: keep answer changes distinct from errors; sham one seed; wrappers architectural; no causal mechanism claim; p=.25 and Holm=.50; 1,918 protection denominator excludes GSM8K; 2,038 literal denominator includes it.\nEOF\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\nx=json.load(open('notes/paper_metadata.json'))\nfor a in x: print(a['id'], a['title'], '; '.join(a['authors']))\nPY\nhead -20 notes/sdf.txt\nhead -20 notes/believe.txt\ncat results/paired_tests.json\nhead -4 results/summary.csv\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
